.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt WATTLE-TEST 1
.Os Wattle DEVEL
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm wattle-test
.Nd run the tests of a project
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm "wattle test"
.Oo
.Ar options
.Oc
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Run the tests.
.Cm test
runs each file ending in
.Ql "\&.wattle"
under
.Ql "\&./test" ,
in a process of its own.
It prints
.Ql "seed:"
and the seed.
It then prints one line for each file,
with a mark,
the path and the counts of tests and assertions.
It prints the output of a file that failed after its line,
each line after a border that is red when colour is on.
It ends with the number of files and tests and the files that
failed.
The output of a file that passed is not printed.
The exit status is 1 if a file failed or no file was run.
A test file that uses the Gum test module,
.Ql "gum/test\&.wattle" ,
reads the dynamic bindings that
.Fl t ,
.Fl T
and
.Fl "-seed"
set.
.Ic t
is a synonym for
.Cm test .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl f ,
.Fl "-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Run only the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path ,
which is relative to
.Ql "\&./test" .
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl F .
.It Xo
.Fl F ,
.Fl "-no-file"
.Ar path
.Xc
Do not run the test file whose path ends with
.Ar path .
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl f .
.It Xo
.Fl t ,
.Fl "-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/tests"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl T .
.It Xo
.Fl T ,
.Fl "-no-test"
.Ar name
.Xc
Add
.Ar name
to the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/skips"
in each test file.
It can be repeated.
It is not compatible with
.Fl t .
.It Xo
.Fl "-seed"
.Ar seed
.Xc
Use the integer
.Ar seed
to seed the generator that shuffles the test files.
Each test file also shuffles its tests with it,
as
.Cm test
sets the dynamic binding
.Ql ":test/seed" .
Without
.Fl "-seed" ,
the seed is taken from the clock,
so each run has a different order.
The same seed gives the same order.
.It Xo
.Fl b ,
.Fl "-bail"
.Xc
Stop after the first test file that fails.
.It Xo
.Fl e ,
.Fl "-lint-error"
.Ar level ,
.Fl w ,
.Fl "-lint-warn"
.Ar level
.Xc
Set the lint levels of each test file.
They take the same values as for
.Ic wattle
.Cm check .
.El
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run the tests in
.Ql "\&./test" ,
skipping one file:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ wattle test --no-file slow\&.wattle
.Ed
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr wattle 1 ,
.Xr wattle-check 1
.
